================================================================================
WHY THE DEVELOP LANE
================================================================================

bERP HRMS tracks upstream's develop lane, and this is deliberate.

bstBizEra/bERP is a fork of ERPNext whose pyproject declares name = "erpnext",
so it occupies the bench's erpnext application slot, and it requires
frappe >=17.0.0-dev,<18.0.0. Every bERP bench is therefore a Frappe 17-dev
bench. This module's frappe >=17.0.0-dev,<18.0.0 and erpnext
>=17.0.0-dev,<18.0.0 match it, as does bstBizEra/bERP-CRM.

Upstream's stable lane (version-16, 16.19.0) requires frappe >=16.0.0,<17.0.0
and erpnext >=16.0.0,<17.0.0. bench compares these with semantic_version, and a
`<17.0.0` bound excludes the 17.0.0-dev prerelease, so the stable lane cannot be
installed onto a bERP bench while the bERP fork holds the erpnext slot.

The trade-off is real: this module is pinned to a moving, unreleased upstream
branch and can break when upstream develop moves. That risk is inherent to the
platform rather than to this module, and it resolves when the whole bERP stack
moves to a released Frappe together.

